    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml-mlx/mlx/tarball/0.12",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml-mlx/mlx/zipball/0.12",
    "body": "CHANGES:\n\n- Add JSX fragments: `<></>`, `<>a b</>` and `<>...xs</>`. A fragment lowers to\n  a list expression with the `[@JSX]` attribute, and `<>...xs</>` lowers to `xs`\n  with `[@JSX]`. A fragment used as a function argument needs parentheses:\n  `f (<>a</>)`.\n- `</>` stays a valid operator, like `<>`, for example `let (</>) a b = a`.\n  Inside a fragment, parenthesize it: `<>(a </> b)</>`.\n- Breaking: operators that start with `<>` followed by `<` or `...`, `</>`\n  followed by `<`, or `>...` (for example `<><`, `<><=`, `>...`) are now split\n  and no longer parse as one operator.\n- Add JSX children spread: `<Foo> ...expr </Foo>` passes `expr` directly as\n  `~children:expr`. The spread must be the only child.\n  [#45](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/45)\n- Fix JSX elements closed directly before `|]` and `}`, such as\n  `[|<div>a</div>|]`. [#46](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/46)\n- Restore unparenthesized expressions in object overrides while keeping JSX\n  closing tags valid directly before record and indexing braces.\n  [#47](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/47)\n- Accept quoted strings with an empty delimiter, `{|...|}`.\n  [#37](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/issues/37)\n- Fix duplicate `children` labels when a JSX element sets `children`\n  explicitly. [#36](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/36)\n- Support OCaml 5.5: the vendored OCaml parser is 5.5.0 and ocamlmerlin-mlx\n  uses merlin 5.8.1-505. mlx still builds with OCaml 4.14 and later.\n- Add Emacs mlx-mode to the editor support list.\n  [#33](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/33)\n"
  },
